<section image-layout="blank" id="3qt0QpLHtM"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="1opVfQguwm" background-color="accent" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">THE INVISIBLE SHIELD CLUB · MISSION 01</p><display size="md">Follow one UV ray</display><h3 role="subheading">Find Earth’s invisible ozone shield.</h3><p font-size="lg">High above the weather, ozone absorbs much of the Sun’s harmful ultraviolet radiation. Today you will spot ozone, predict what changes and explain how people protect it.</p><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="TbOP6Ul2ai" background-color="palette-3" padding="12pt 16pt"><p font-size="18pt"><b>MISSION</b> Spot O₃ → predict UV → protect together.</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="EKu4fLlo7k" background-color="surface" padding="8pt 12pt"><p role="caption">Source: <a href="https://www.unep.org/news-and-stories/press-release/ozone-layer-recovery-track-helping-avoid-global-warming-05degc">UNEP ozone assessment</a></p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="7v4WM39aqT" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/H0HMR0HoI1NmcAWHrHsyc.png" saved-media-id="r6l8a8p1w4xlhdg" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="atmosphere-cut-paper" alt="Layered cut-paper editorial science illustration of Earth curving across the lower right, cloud-white land beneath a thin shield-blue atmospheric arc, several UV-gold sunlight paths arriving from the upper left with some ending in the blue region and some continuing, deep-ink outer space, clean vector-like edges, subtle paper fibers, bright optimistic mood, no text or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="lqrsvuutJZ" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="eKBuCula7u"><h2>Meet ozone: three oxygen atoms</h2><grid spacing="large"><grid-item id="Oxw9pR7csX" vertical-align="center" colspan="22"><p font-size="lg">Ozone is <b>O₃</b>: three oxygen atoms joined together. Most protective ozone is in the <b>stratosphere</b>, above our weather.</p><p font-size="lg">It is a spread-out region of gas, not a solid shell. Ozone near the ground is a separate air-pollution problem.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="swhEUOzs1b" vertical-align="center" colspan="38"><freeform-block w="500" h="120"><shape preset="line" x="103" y="51" w="22" h="2" stroke="palette-4" stroke-width="5"></shape><shape preset="line" x="203" y="51" w="22" h="2" stroke="palette-4" stroke-width="5"></shape><box type="content" x="25" y="12" w="78" h="78" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="accent" style="border-radius: 999pt;"><h3 align="center">O</h3></box><box type="content" x="125" y="12" w="78" h="78" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="accent" style="border-radius: 999pt;"><h3 align="center">O</h3></box><box type="content" x="225" y="12" w="78" h="78" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="accent" style="border-radius: 999pt;"><h3 align="center">O</h3></box><box type="content" x="320" y="30" w="170"><p font-size="18pt"><b>O₃</b><br>one ozone molecule</p></box></freeform-block><grid divider="sm palette-5" direction="vertical" spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="I_keCqpG0I" background-color="palette-4" padding="10pt 14pt"><h4>STRATOSPHERE</h4><p font-size="18pt">A region of gas above the weather.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="6jVjvbnFpP" background-color="accent" padding="10pt 14pt"><h4>PROTECTIVE OZONE REGION</h4><p font-size="18pt">O₃ is spread through the air—not a solid wall.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="B3k7mEepTj" background-color="surface" padding="10pt 14pt"><h4>WEATHER BELOW</h4><p font-size="18pt">Clouds and weather happen lower down, near Earth’s surface.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="RNiNDCAzSN"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="k1ar4jpiBP"><h2>Predict the UV path</h2><p font-size="18pt"><b>Same Sun. Same three incoming UV rays. Same Earth.</b> Only the amount of stratospheric ozone changes. Which ground receives less harmful UV?</p><freeform-block w="840" h="275"><box type="content" w="405" h="258" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="border-radius: 18pt;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="435" w="405" h="258" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="border-radius: 18pt;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="24" y="12" w="220"><h3>More ozone</h3><p font-size="16pt">5 ozone dots in this model</p></box><box type="content" x="459" y="12" w="220"><h3>Less ozone</h3><p font-size="16pt">2 ozone dots in this model</p></box><shape preset="ellipse" x="35" y="70" w="50" h="50" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="470" y="70" w="50" h="50" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="line" x="130" y="76" w="2" h="82" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="202" y="76" w="2" h="82" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="274" y="76" w="2" h="82" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="565" y="76" w="2" h="82" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="637" y="76" w="2" h="82" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="709" y="76" w="2" h="82" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><box type="content" x="38" y="154" w="329" h="24" sizing="fixed" background-color="accent" style="border-radius: 999pt;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="473" y="154" w="329" h="24" sizing="fixed" background-color="accent" style="border-radius: 999pt;"><p></p></box><shape preset="ellipse" x="80" y="158" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="122" y="158" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="164" y="158" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="266" y="158" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="308" y="158" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="557" y="158" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="749" y="158" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><box type="content" x="88" y="194" w="225" h="72" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="border-radius: 999pt;"><h3 align="center">?</h3><p font-size="16pt" align="center">harmful UV at the ground</p></box><box type="content" x="523" y="194" w="225" h="72" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="border-radius: 999pt;"><h3 align="center">?</h3><p font-size="16pt" align="center">harmful UV at the ground</p></box></freeform-block><p font-size="lg"><b>Point, vote and explain your reason.</b></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="19308SiV8o"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="oBNwTaEGl_"><h2>Reveal: what the ozone region changes</h2><freeform-block w="840" h="275"><box type="content" w="405" h="258" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="border-radius: 18pt;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="435" w="405" h="258" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="border-radius: 18pt;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="24" y="12" w="220"><h3>More ozone</h3><p font-size="16pt">5 ozone dots in this model</p></box><box type="content" x="459" y="12" w="220"><h3>Less ozone</h3><p font-size="16pt">2 ozone dots in this model</p></box><shape preset="ellipse" x="35" y="70" w="50" h="50" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="470" y="70" w="50" h="50" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="line" x="130" y="76" w="2" h="82" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="202" y="76" w="2" h="82" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="274" y="76" w="2" h="82" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="565" y="76" w="2" h="82" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="637" y="76" w="2" h="82" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="709" y="76" w="2" h="82" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><box type="content" x="38" y="154" w="329" h="24" sizing="fixed" background-color="accent" style="border-radius: 999pt;"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="473" y="154" w="329" h="24" sizing="fixed" background-color="accent" style="border-radius: 999pt;"><p></p></box><shape preset="ellipse" x="80" y="158" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="122" y="158" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="164" y="158" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="266" y="158" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="308" y="158" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="557" y="158" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="ellipse" x="749" y="158" w="16" h="16" fill="surface" stroke-width="0"></shape><shape preset="line" x="202" y="178" w="2" h="34" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="637" y="178" w="2" h="34" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><shape preset="line" x="709" y="178" w="2" h="34" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="4"></shape><box type="content" x="88" y="201" w="225" h="67" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="border-radius: 999pt;"><h4 align="center">More is absorbed</h4><p font-size="16pt" align="center">Less harmful UV reaches the ground.</p></box><box type="content" x="523" y="201" w="225" h="67" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-5" style="border-radius: 999pt;"><h4 align="center">Less is absorbed</h4><p font-size="16pt" align="center">More harmful UV reaches the ground.</p></box></freeform-block><p font-size="lg"><b>Ozone changes the amount of harmful UV. It does not block every ray.</b></p><p role="caption">Conceptual ray paths; counts are illustrative. Source: <a href="https://www.unep.org/news-and-stories/press-release/ozone-layer-recovery-track-helping-avoid-global-warming-05degc">UNEP ozone assessment</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="HueUPtAF2t"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Zb8ZzNdkB7"><h2>How one reactive atom can repeat the damage</h2><p font-size="18pt">Long-lived human-made gases can reach the stratosphere, where sunlight starts a repeating ozone-damaging chain.</p><freeform-block w="840" h="230"><box type="content" x="25" y="8" w="120" h="120" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="accent" style="border-radius: 999pt;"><h3 align="center">ODS<br>↑</h3></box><box type="content" x="245" y="8" w="120" h="120" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-2" style="border-radius: 999pt;"><h3 align="center">UV</h3></box><box type="content" x="465" y="8" w="120" h="120" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="border-radius: 999pt;"><h3 align="center">O₃ + <span text-color="accent">●</span></h3></box><box type="content" x="685" y="8" w="120" h="120" vertical-align="center" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-3" style="border-radius: 999pt;"><h3 align="center">↺</h3></box><box type="content" x="174" y="42" w="42"><h1 align="center">→</h1></box><box type="content" x="394" y="42" w="42"><h1 align="center">→</h1></box><box type="content" x="614" y="42" w="42"><h1 align="center">→</h1></box><box type="content" y="145" w="170"><h4 align="center">Linger and rise</h4><p font-size="18pt" align="center">The chemicals can stay for years.</p></box><box type="content" x="220" y="145" w="170"><h4 align="center">UV opens them</h4><p font-size="18pt" align="center">A reactive atom is released.</p></box><box type="content" x="440" y="145" w="170"><h4 align="center">Meet ozone</h4><p font-size="18pt" align="center">The chain reduces ozone.</p></box><box type="content" x="660" y="145" w="180"><h4 align="center">Act again</h4><p font-size="18pt" align="center">The damaging chain can repeat.</p></box></freeform-block><aside variant="info"><p>Simplified chain: the full chemistry has more steps, but the ozone-damaging process can repeat.</p></aside><p font-size="11pt">Source: <a href="https://ozone.unep.org/treaties/montreal-protocol">UNEP, Montreal Protocol</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="lRYk8do10V"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="jocRN2P1k7"><h2>The comeback has a clock</h2><p>If current policies stay in place, a 2023 UN-backed assessment projects a return to 1980 ozone levels at different times.</p><smart-layout variant="minimalTimeline" orientation="horizontal" cell-size="15"><smart-layout-item><h4>Around 2040 · Global</h4><p>Ozone levels across most of the world could return first.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Around 2045 · Arctic</h4><p>Recovery near the North Pole is projected a little later.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Around 2066 · Antarctic</h4><p>Recovery near the South Pole is expected to take longest.</p></smart-layout-item></smart-layout><aside variant="success"><p>These are projections, not guaranteed dates. Continuing the plan matters.</p></aside><p font-size="sm">Source: <a href="https://www.unep.org/news-and-stories/press-release/ozone-layer-recovery-track-helping-avoid-global-warming-05degc">UNEP, 2023 assessment</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="t4ZxBoTxf-"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="MfhNM8-B5r"><h2>Different actions do different jobs</h2><p font-size="18pt"><b>Call out O, S or C for each tile:</b> ozone recovery, sun safety or climate action. Be ready to explain why.</p><grid spacing="small"><grid-item id="OeEMAGGiTp" cell-style="outline" padding="12pt 16pt" colspan="20"><p font-size="18pt"><b>A</b> Countries phase out ozone-depleting chemicals.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="11df_VJl8z" cell-style="outline" padding="12pt 16pt" colspan="20"><p font-size="18pt"><b>B</b> A trained technician services an old cooling unit.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="P9l2pcvFle" cell-style="outline" padding="12pt 16pt" colspan="20"><p font-size="18pt"><b>C</b> Wear a hat and seek shade.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ajZkHc6U-9" cell-style="outline" padding="12pt 16pt" colspan="20"><p font-size="18pt"><b>D</b> Use sunscreen as directed.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="oLJchbuwPj" cell-style="outline" padding="12pt 16pt" colspan="20"><p font-size="18pt"><b>E</b> Ask adults to choose lower-warming cooling options.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="4wIKpzA2K_" cell-style="outline" padding="12pt 16pt" colspan="20"><p font-size="18pt"><b>F</b> Save energy at home or school.</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="dp_Fur9vW9" background-color="palette-3" padding="12pt 16pt" colspan="20"><h3>O · Ozone recovery</h3><p font-size="18pt">Cuts ozone-depleting substances.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="t4IWU50coE" background-color="palette-2" padding="12pt 16pt" colspan="20"><h3>S · Sun safety</h3><p font-size="18pt">Protects skin from UV now.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="HrmAVrEEUP" background-color="accent" padding="12pt 16pt" colspan="20"><h3>C · Climate action</h3><p font-size="18pt">Reduces warming—a different job.</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="Um0Jt8jGOm" vertical-align="center" colspan="48"><p font-size="18pt"><b>Remember:</b> HFCs do not deplete ozone, but many can warm the climate.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="NJdoXZhlKj" vertical-align="center" text-color="#486875" colspan="12"><p role="caption" align="right">Source: <a href="https://www.unep.org/news-and-stories/press-release/ozone-layer-recovery-track-helping-avoid-global-warming-05degc">UNEP</a></p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><notes><p>Sorting key: A and B = ozone recovery. C and D = sun safety. E and F = climate action. Emphasize that children should not handle refrigerants or service cooling equipment; that work belongs to trained adults.</p></notes></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="5s82U58uaU" background-color="palette-4"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="XgYs3KvHvV" background-color="palette-4" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">TEACH IT BACK</p><h1 font-size="36pt">Your 20-second shield story</h1><grid divider="sm palette-5" marker="number" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="inline" direction="vertical" spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-inline-size: 30pt; --marker-gap: 12pt;"><grid-item id="McqTWVnuN3" padding="7pt 0"><p font-size="18pt"><b>Where?</b> In the stratosphere, above the weather.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="IjTi_vPBtC" padding="7pt 0"><p font-size="18pt"><b>Its job?</b> Absorb much harmful UV; some still passes.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="Nv2ptvmcJG" padding="7pt 0"><p font-size="18pt"><b>What thinned it?</b> Long-lived human-made chemicals.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="m2TxOvpbiX" padding="7pt 0"><p font-size="18pt"><b>What helps?</b> Countries phasing those chemicals out together.</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="Sw7xVdJPJq" background-color="palette-3" padding="12pt 16pt"><h4>Finish strong</h4><p font-size="18pt">Name one real action, then correct one mix-up: sun safety protects people now; it does not repair ozone.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="5xBM1D6WpK" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/U-xDlB-5f2pctyAXHy_52.png" saved-media-id="eg2qgh3t3r7vfnx" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="atmosphere-cut-paper" alt="Layered cut-paper editorial science illustration of a curious ten-year-old pointing toward an Earth cutaway at the lower right, the Earth in the same orientation as a curved cloud-white surface beneath a thin shield-blue atmospheric arc, UV-gold rays arriving from the upper left with some stopping in the arc and one continuing, a small action-green circle suggesting cooperation, deep-ink space, clean vector-like edges, subtle paper fibers, confident optimistic classroom tone, no text or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>